# Agentic Workspace — Cursor (Unified, Ticket-Folder Workflow)

> Cursor always-on project context (equivalent role to root `CLAUDE.md` for Claude Code).
> Canonical SDD source lives under `agentic/`; install with `scripts/setup-agentic.sh cursor`.
> Project overlays (any name — no naming-prefix convention) stay in IDE runtime dirs and are
> **outside** the required orchestrator.
>
> The **shared, IDE-agnostic** SDD contract (workspace identity, ticket folder, personas, pipeline,
> confidence scoring, multi-repo, knowledge base, skills, hooks (purpose), session memory, metrics,
> MCP, error protocol) lives in root `AGENTS.md` (source: `agentic/AGENTS.md`) — Cursor reads it
> natively alongside this rule file; it is **not** repeated here. Everything below is specific to
> Cursor and intentionally lives only here.

## Where things live (Cursor)

| Kind | Path |
|------|------|
| Subagents / personas | `.cursor/agents/beacon/` |
| Framework skills | `.cursor/skills/beacon/` |
| Project overlays | `.agents/{agents,commands,skills}/` (any name; Cursor skills load from here, agents/commands are linked flat into `.cursor/`, outside `beacon/`) |
| Hooks | `.cursor/hooks.json` + `.cursor/hooks/beacon/` |
| Canonical source | `agentic/` (edit here, then re-run setup) |

## Personas — Cursor invocation

Invoke via Task / agent defs under `.cursor/agents/beacon/`, or slash skills where present (e.g.
`/run` → `.cursor/skills/beacon/run`). See `AGENTS.md` for the full persona table (roles, inputs).

## Flat orchestration

Subagents must not nest Task. Main session only. `/run` follows
`agentic/skills/run-pipeline/SKILL.md`.

**Spec updates are `Task(do)`-only:** the main session never directly patches a spec file
(`apply_patch`, bulk search-replace, or any other direct edit) for checkbox/status/`_state.json`
bookkeeping. Personas return **Proposed spec updates**; once the matching `Task(scrum)` gate
returns **PROCEED**, the orchestrator delegates a batched `Task(do)` to apply them — `Task(scrum)`
PROCEED authorizes `Task(do)`, never a direct orchestrator patch.

## Model Selection (Cursor)

Every agent's canonical frontmatter is `model: inherit` (see `AGENTS.md`'s general note — no
hardcoded economy tier, since available model tiers vary per environment). Two independent
override mechanisms exist here:

- **Per-install (own file, same mechanism as Claude Code):** `agentic/models/cursor.yml` (copy from
  `agentic/models/example.yml`, gitignored) — `scripts/setup-agentic.sh cursor` rewrites the
  installed `.cursor/agents/beacon/*.md` copy's `model:` line for any agent listed. Claude Code reads its
  **own** `agentic/models/claude.yml` — same checkout, independent overrides per IDE.
- **Dynamic per-step (Cursor-only, pre-existing):** `.cursor/models.yml` (team baseline) or
  `.cursor/models.user.yml` (`use_manual_models: true` for manual assignment), applied at runtime
  by `scripts/tools/apply-models.sh` during `/run`. Neither file is tracked by default.

The per-install file sets the static default; the dynamic mechanism can still override per pipeline
step on top of it.

## Error highlights

Missing ticket folder → search `docs/specs/`. Two control files (`context.json` + `_state.json`) →
stop (AC-1). Hook failures fail-open except protected-branch writes (always refused). Full error
protocol: `AGENTS.md`.
